From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: fix the OCI check of a Link Reconfiguration Request

hostapd_handle_link_reconf_req() treats the return value of
ocv_verify_tx_params() as true on success, but OCI_SUCCESS is 0. A
Link Reconfiguration Request with a valid OCI is dropped, and one with
an invalid OCI passes. Compare against OCI_SUCCESS, and take the transmit
parameters of the station on the link, as the SA Query check does.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -2834,6 +2834,8 @@ hostapd_handle_link_reconf_req(struct ho
 		}
 	} else {
 		struct wpa_channel_info ci;
+		int tx_chanwidth;
+		int tx_seg1_idx;
 
 		if (!wpa_auth_uses_ocv(assoc_sta->wpa_sm)) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
@@ -2847,9 +2849,16 @@ hostapd_handle_link_reconf_req(struct ho
 			goto out;
 		}
 
-		if (!ocv_verify_tx_params(elems.oci, elems.oci_len, &ci,
+		if (get_sta_tx_parameters(assoc_sta->wpa_sm,
+					  hostapd_mld_link_id(hapd),
 					  channel_width_to_int(ci.chanwidth),
-					  ci.seg1_idx)) {
+					  ci.seg1_idx, &tx_chanwidth,
+					  &tx_seg1_idx) < 0)
+			goto out;
+
+		if (ocv_verify_tx_params(elems.oci, elems.oci_len, &ci,
+					 tx_chanwidth, tx_seg1_idx) !=
+		    OCI_SUCCESS) {
 			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
 				   "MLD: OCI verification failed; drop Link Reconfiguration Request");
 			goto out;
